Third-party native components bundled for the on-device computer (COS)
======================================================================

Modified: 2026-11-04 (dynamic-section edits listed below; files shipped
unstripped, byte-identical to the "Shipped .so sha256" list).

The APK ships these unmodified-source, prebuilt Termux binaries in
lib/<abi>/ (jniLibs, ABIs arm64-v8a and x86_64). They were taken from the
Termux main apt repository, renamed to lib*.so so Android installs them into
nativeLibraryDir (the only exec-able app location under W^X), and their ELF
dynamic sections were edited with patchelf. No code was changed:
  libproot.so (bin/proot)      RUNPATH /data/data/com.termux/files/usr/lib -> $ORIGIN
                               DT_NEEDED libtalloc.so.2 -> libtalloc.so
  libtalloc.so (libtalloc.so.2.5.0)
                               RUNPATH /data/data/com.termux/files/usr/lib -> $ORIGIN
                               DT_SONAME libtalloc.so.2 -> libtalloc.so
  libandroid-shmem.so          RUNPATH /data/data/com.termux/files/usr/lib removed
  libproot-loader.so           (libexec/proot/loader) byte-identical to the .deb
The build keeps these files unstripped (packaging.jniLibs.keepDebugSymbols).
Corresponding sources are linked below (GPL-2.0 §3 / LGPL-3.0 §4).

